e paper; this will be formally introduced in the next section. By a careful analysis of the extremal cases of this result, we will obtain the following theorem, the case 𝑟 =𝑘 of which shows that (the modified) Fischer's conjecture holds for any sufficiently large graph. Note that the graph Γ𝑛,𝑟,𝑘 in the statement is defined in Construction 1.2.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nExtremal Theorems for Degree Sequence Packing and the Two-Color Discrete Tomography Problem (https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/140987912)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.0 years ago; Crawled: 2.4 years ago; Wenger, On the sum necessary to ensure a degree sequence is potentially $H$-graphic, Combinatorica, to appear. ... Hajnal and E. Szemerédi, Proof of a conjecture of Erdös, in Combinatorial Theory and Its Applications, II, P.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Degree Sequence Komlós Theorem (https://epubs.siam.org/doi/abs/10.1137/18M1197102?casa_token=w3o8Y49lYQwAAAAA%3A6hciaHE6nxEyZZGKjbF4ut0Jlm2hJdh5GMGqAIVM89SkOtYrEbcty7QjzGbM6BYbHb0F52IAcw&journalCode=sjdmec)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.1 years ago; Crawled: 2.4 years ago; An important result of Komlós [Tiling Turán theorems, Combinatorica, 2000] yields the asymptotically exact minimum degree threshold that ensures a graph $G$ contains an $H$-tiling covering an $x$th proportion of the vertices of $G$ (for any fixed $x \\in (0,1)$ and graph $H$). ... Szemerédi, Proof of a conjecture of Erdös, Combin. ... Treglown, A degree sequence Hajnal-Szemerédi theorem, J.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAndrew Treglown - Summer School in Graph Coloring (https://web.mat.bham.ac.uk/A.Treglown/summerschool)\nciteturn1search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.9 years ago; Crawled: 3.5 years ago; Lecture 3: an exact result ...   * The proof of the approximate Ba